{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-27T19:45:03.267Z","data":{"text":"Done. Task 1 is complete.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `src/core/report/result-sections.ts` — rewrote `cleanSection` to implement the new \"says only `None`\" rule: a section is absent when it has exactly one non-blank line that, after dropping a leading list marker (`-`, `*`, `+`, or `<n>.`) and setting aside every `*` and `_`, is `None` alone or followed straight away by `.`, `;`, `,`, or `:` and any text. Present text is still returned trimmed unchanged. `checkBlocked`/`readChangeDisclosures` inherit the fix via the shared parser, so no caller changed.\n- `tests/result-none-sections.test.ts` — new tests for every \"Result file sections\" scenario (headings, blocked, bullet/bold, explanations, sentence starting with `None`, and multi-line via `readChangeDisclosures`) plus the watcher \"Blocked says None as a bullet\" scenario through `runWatcherOnce`.\n\n**Verified:**\n- Task verify: `node --import tsx --test tests/result-none-sections.test.ts` — 7/7 pass.\n- Preexisting `tests/result-sections.test.ts` and `tests/blocked-exit.test.ts` pass unchanged.\n- Proposal verify: `pnpm verify` — green (typechecks, build, full suite, lint).\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/103-result-none-sections/.run/results/1.md`."}}
